{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 31, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJust back from two weeks in Japan, and I'm already dreaming of going back! It was a whirlwind of ancient temples, bustling cityscapes, and incredible food.\n\nMy trip started in Tokyo, a sensory overload in the best way. Shibuya Crossing was everything I imagined – a chaotic ballet of people. I explored quirky Harajuku, marveled at the Imperial Palace, and spent hours getting delightfully lost in the electric Akihabara district.\n\nNext, I took the shinkansen (bullet train!) to Kyoto. The contrast was stunning. Here, I wandered through serene bamboo forests, visited golden pavilions like Kinkaku-ji, and experienced a traditional tea ceremony.  Gion, the geisha district, felt like stepping back in time.\n\nFood was a highlight, of course. From delicate sushi and ramen to savory okonomiyaki and takoyaki, every meal was an adventure. I even braved a conveyor belt sushi restaurant!\n\nNavigating the public transport was surprisingly easy, and the politeness of everyone I encountered was truly heartwarming.  While I definitely felt like a tourist at times, I felt welcomed and safe throughout my journey.\n\nJapan is a country of beautiful contradictions – ancient traditions seamlessly blending with cutting-edge technology. It’s a place that will challenge your perceptions and leave you wanting more.  Highly recommend adding it to your travel bucket list!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0012646066024899483}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.16978870332241058}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0015025765169411898}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.1128273531794548}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.11438143253326416}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.16682948172092438}, {"toke